(NOVATECH BRAND GOVERNANCE AND COMPLIANCE MANUAL 2026) '
(DOCUMENT SPECIFICATION: ENTERPRISE GLOBAL EDITION) '
() '
(SECTION 1: BRAND IDENTITY AND TONE OF VOICE) '
(Our brand voice is professional, empowering, collaborative, and grounded in engineering rigor.) '
(- Rule TV-01: Communicate with clarity and empathy. Avoid condescending, combative, or aggressive language.) '
(- Rule TV-02: Never use high-pressure sales gimmicks or create artificial scarcity in any campaign.) '
(- Rule TV-03: Use active voice and concise phrasing. Prioritize customer empowerment over corporate hype.) '
() '
(SECTION 2: PROHIBITED CLAIMS AND RESTRICTED VOCABULARY) '
(The following terms and claim patterns are strictly forbidden across all public marketing channels:) '
(- Rule PC-01: Prohibited term: 'cheap'. Use 'cost-effective' or 'competitively priced' instead.) '
(- Rule PC-02: Prohibited term: '100% bug-free'. No software is bug-free. Use 'rigorously tested and stable'.) '
(- Rule PC-03: Prohibited term: 'guaranteed 100% uptime'. Our certified SLA is 99.9%, never 100%.) '
(- Rule PC-04: Prohibited term: 'miracle fix'. Avoid sensationalist promises. Use 'comprehensive workflow solution'.) '
(- Rule PC-05: Prohibited phrase: 'crush the competition'. Combative framing violates our collaborative positioning.) '
(- Rule PC-06: Prohibited term: 'unlimited forever'. Do not make uncapped perpetual licensing commitments.) '
(- Rule PC-07: Prohibited term: 'military-grade'. Vague security hyperbole is disallowed by compliance boards.) '
ET
endstream
